 is about 50bp of cuts.\n- **CMA's own view:** Governor Ashby said on 28 October that one 25bp cut in 2027 is the base case. She also said markets \"may be getting ahead of themselves.\" The market is therefore pricing about 25bp more easing than the CMA signals.\n- **Sensitivity of the multiple:** The factsheet says the basket's forward P/E is 19x. A 50bp lower policy path has historically lifted that P/E by about 1.5 points. If the CMA's path is the one that plays out, about 0.75 point (roughly 4%) of the 19x may already reflect cuts that don't happen. That is a modest de-rating risk. It matters only if the 19x was built on the market-implied path.\n- **Earnings:** Consensus expects 2027 EPS growth of 14%, driven by backlog conversion at Voltaris (14% of the fund) and Tarnwell (11%). Estimates are up 3% over the past quarter. A 4% multiple compression against 14% EPS growth still leaves roughly 9–10% price upside through 2027, if the 14% is delivered.\n- **Risks:** Voltaris and Tarnwell are 25% of the fund, so the earnings case rests on two names. The 19x is already a growth multiple, so there is little cushion if backlog conversion slips and the CMA also stays hawkish.\n\nI did not check the 19x against a historical range. I also did not test whether the 19x already embeds the market path.","ttft_ms":3736,"type":"result","duration_ms":28054,"uuid":"a2b6e6f5-b808-4524-9bba-2e8e18db842d","ttft_stream_ms":3143,"time_to_request_ms":62,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_req